{
  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-MATERIAL-INTERFACE-RIEMANN-DATA-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "direct judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "direct judge classification is undetermined",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D003 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "Classify the target as not-faithful-weaker. It establishes a valid componentwise data identity, but that identity does not recover the selected characterization involving discontinuities in both material and state. This conclusion does not depend on deciding whether the source implicitly assumes piecewise homogeneous media.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 8, first paragraph, specifies a discontinuity in the medium at zero together with an initial-data discontinuity. The elaborated target contains only an equivalence between three applications of D001; D001 contains half-line equalities without distinctness or a discontinuity condition."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The source-to-target direction is confirmed. The reverse direction fails as a complete semantic representation of the selected setup. The direct judge correctly identified the product identity and the unresolved global medium model; the latter uncertainty need not prevent rejection on the independent discontinuity-coverage defect.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.11) on printed page 5 supplies constant initial-state cases. Printed page 8 adds the material discontinuity. The target and D001 supply only the componentwise constancy identity."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The weaker classification is supported, but some supporting arguments require qualification. An unconditional equivalence can faithfully formalize a definition, so its truth when both sides are false is not by itself a defect. Likewise, omission of solution dynamics is appropriate here. The substantive issue is that neither side characterizes both actual discontinuities.",
      "primary_evidence": "The selected sentence on printed page 8 concerns extension of the setup; wave decomposition and reflection/transmission appear in the following sentence. D001 and the blind translation contain no requirement distinguishing genuine jumps from equal-side profiles."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Resolve the classification to not-faithful-weaker while retaining uncertainty about the source's global medium model. Even granting a piecewise constant medium interpretation, satisfaction of the encoded data conditions does not imply discontinuities in both components.",
      "primary_evidence": "With Material = State = Real, medium constantly 1 and initialState constantly 0, and matching equal left/right values, both sides of the target equivalence hold. Neither field has a discontinuity, unlike the selected configuration on printed page 8."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "D001 is fully understood: it specifies exact constancy on each open half-line and nothing at zero. Its initial-state assignments agree with equation (1.11). Its application to medium imposes the same global constancy pattern, and it does not require unequal side values for either field. Thus its meaning is settled; its medium-domain correspondence remains partly unspecified by the source.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001's supplied body is the conjunction of universal implications x < 0 → data x = leftState and 0 < x → data x = rightState. Printed page 5 displays these state assignments; printed pages 7–8 discuss material jumps without an explicit global coefficient formula."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D003 unclear",
      "resolution": "D003 is logical equivalence. In this target both directions follow from equality of ordered pairs being coordinatewise. D002 conjoins the half-line and component conditions; D004–D005 construct the product; D007 supplies exact equality. These dependencies preserve separate material and state roles but add no discontinuity semantics. Their reused meanings have been reassessed for this target.",
      "primary_evidence": "The explicit target pairs medium x with initialState x and the corresponding side values. D001 expands both sides into exactly the same four component equalities, regrouped by conjunction."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The real spatial domain, separate component types, and treatment of initialState as a time-zero slice are appropriate. Arbitrary codomains are harmless for the equality identity and are not independently a binder defect. They do, however, provide no interpretation of topological discontinuity; that missing semantic link cannot be inferred from binder names.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 uses real vector-valued states, and equation (1.11) evaluates them at time zero. The target has arbitrary Material and State with no structure. D006 supplies Real; D008 and D010 supply strict real order; D009, D011, and D012 interpret the shared boundary as real zero."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "For this selected data-setup claim, an explicit evolution equation need not occur in a representation lemma, and no additional existence or interface law should be demanded. However, the target has neither side-value distinctness nor another condition identifying both components as genuinely discontinuous. This is a substantive mismatch with the selected prose, even though degenerate cases are algebraically legitimate.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5 defines the full Riemann problem using a hyperbolic equation and initial data. Printed page 8's selected sentence specifies both discontinuities, while the subsequent sentence concerns solving the problem. The target and D001 include no distinctness or discontinuity condition."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target preserves the initial-state half-lines, common origin, and separate material/state roles. It does not completely characterize the selected discontinuous configuration. No neighboring declaration supplies missing target semantics merely by being imported: IsRiemannInitialValueSolution is absent from the elaborated target and its semantic dependency inventory.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete target type uses only IsRiemannData, pairs, and logical connectives. Printed page 8 specifies coincident discontinuities. The supplied dependency inventory contains no equation predicate or additional interface predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The internal equivalence is exact, with correct equality and strict inequality directions. The failure is not that the source lacks explicit iff notation or that the theorem does not assert an arbitrary supplied function satisfies its predicates. The failure is that the predicates being equated omit a defining feature of the selected configuration: discontinuities in both components.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 uses the same strict inequalities as equation (1.11), and pair equality splits into component equalities. Nevertheless, both predicates admit continuously constant real-valued material and state fields, whereas printed page 8 describes both fields as discontinuous."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The codomain generalization gives a valid and nonvacuous algebraic identity. It does not make this a faithful-stronger theorem about material-interface configurations. If the medium's global half-line constancy is an additional restriction relative to the source, that restricts applicability of the proposed encoding rather than strengthening the source result. Whether the source intends that restriction remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 7 discusses both smoothly varying heterogeneity and sharp material interfaces. Printed page 8 motivates interface problems using cell material properties but gives no global medium formula. D001 medium requires a single prescribed material value on each entire open half-line."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Leaving both values at zero unconstrained matches the source. Equal-side cases are permitted by the displayed state template, so their admission alone does not invalidate every generalization of equation (1.11). Here, however, the target offers no distinction between those cases and the two genuine discontinuities selected on page 8. Even a nonconstant paired profile need not have jumps in both components.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.11) omits zero and does not display q_l ≠ q_r. Printed page 8 explicitly describes both discontinuities. Taking a constant real-valued medium and an initial state with left value 0 and right value 1 satisfies both target predicates while only the state jumps."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve this implication to no. The target provides a reusable encoding identity but no bridge from that encoding to the selected pair of actual discontinuities. Nonvacuity is confirmed: real-valued medium data with sides 1 and 2 and state data with sides 0 and 1 satisfy both predicates with genuine jumps. The existence of those intended instances does not make the encoded predicate equivalent to the source configuration.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 permits both the nontrivial two-jump example and the constant or single-jump examples. Printed page 8 selects coincident medium and initial-data discontinuities. No supplied target dependency distinguishes those examples."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "The target proves that paired half-line constancy is equivalent to separate half-line constancy. Even assuming these predicates hold, neither a material jump nor a state jump follows: constant real-valued functions with equal prescribed side values satisfy them. A constant medium paired with a jumping state also satisfies them. Thus the proposed characterization does not recover the selected configuration involving both discontinuities. This is a semantic insufficiency of the represented predicates, not an objection to equivalences as a form of definition or a demand for the subsequent wave-dynamics theorem."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "In the ordinary mathematical background, the target follows independently of the source assumptions: equality of two ordered pairs is equivalent to the two component equalities, and the universal half-line conditions regroup by conjunction. Consequently the source also entails this identity. This does not imply that every source medium satisfies the half-line constancy predicate, nor that the source supplies a global piecewise constant medium model."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected passage does not settle whether its extended Riemann medium is globally constant on each half-line or may vary away from the material interface. The cell-based motivation supports a piecewise homogeneous interpretation but does not explicitly prescribe it.",
    "Equation (1.11) omits explicit inequality of the initial side states. The source does not specify a formal convention for including degenerate equal-state configurations. This uncertainty does not supply the missing characterization of both discontinuities in the selected sentence."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "incomplete-discontinuity-characterization",
      "evidence": "Printed page 8 selects discontinuities in both medium and initial data. D001 specifies only half-line constancy, and the target only distributes this predicate over a product. Both predicates can hold for constant real-valued fields or for a constant medium paired with a jumping state.",
      "impact": "The target does not recover the selected two-discontinuity configuration and is not accepted as a complete faithful formalization."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "unresolved-medium-model-scope",
      "evidence": "Printed pages 7–8 discuss material heterogeneity and interfaces without displaying a global coefficient profile. D001 applied to medium requires constant values throughout both open half-lines.",
      "impact": "The proposed representation may cover only a piecewise homogeneous specialization. This uncertainty remains, but resolving it favorably would not repair the independent discontinuity-coverage defect."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-and-scope-correction",
      "evidence": "Distinct real-valued side data provide nontrivial satisfying instances. Equation (1.11) leaves zero free, as does D001. The selected sentence precedes the separate wave-decomposition claim.",
      "impact": "The theorem is a valid, nonvacuous representation lemma. Its elementary nature, unrestricted zero values, and omission of subsequent solution dynamics are not defects by themselves."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Inspection of the attached primary-source pages and the supplied statement evidence confirms the blind translation and all dependency meanings. The target correctly preserves coordinatewise equalities, side orientation, the common origin, separate material/state roles, and free interface values. It nevertheless equates predicates that do not characterize both discontinuities required by the selected prose. Source-to-Lean holds as an elementary logical consequence; the reverse semantic coverage fails. The resulting classification is not-faithful-weaker, independently of the remaining ambiguity about the medium's global profile. No tools were used and no provenance hashes were independently recomputed."
}
